-- DO NOT RUN. NEUTRALISED 2026-09-03. Renamed off `.sql` so no runner or glob can
-- pick it up, and every statement below is commented out. Kept, not deleted: the
-- five UIDs it names are genuinely ours and the record of them is worth having.
-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- THE UIDS ARE REAL. Re-verified on Base Sepolia 2026-09-03: all five resolve,
-- minted by this system's own attester under its own schema, on-chain timestamps
-- matching their rows to within a minute. Unlike the 2026-06-03 file beside this
-- one, nothing here borrows another project's evidence. That file is the reason
-- the guard exists; this one is a different and subtler failure.
--
-- THE FAILURE IS THAT THE SQL DOES NOT IMPLEMENT ITS OWN HEADER. The comments map
-- each UID to a specific proof id, agent and tier. The statements do not: each is
--
--     WHERE merkle_root = <batch root> AND eas_attestation_uid IS NULL LIMIT 1
--
-- an UNORDERED predicate with LIMIT 1. Which UID lands on which row is whatever
-- the planner returns. A documented mapping that the code does not enforce is a
-- claim nobody is checking.
--
-- AND TODAY IT WOULD RELIABLY HIT THE WRONG ROWS [MEASURED 2026-09-03]. The five
-- rows the header names already carry these UIDs, so `AND eas_attestation_uid IS
-- NULL` now EXCLUDES exactly its intended targets. Thousands of other rows share
-- that batch merkle root and have no UID, so a run today would attach five real
-- attestations to five arbitrary OTHER proofs — and the mapping in this header
-- would silently become false. The guard clause was written assuming the targets
-- were empty; they are not, so it now selects against its own intent.
--
-- NOT ONE ROW UNDER THAT MERKLE ROOT IS REAL. Every proof sharing it is
-- `is_real = false`. So the whole batch this file exists to "drive anchored from
-- 5 to >=10" is simulated, and raising a count of anchored proofs by stamping
-- more simulated rows raises the number without raising the evidence. That is the
-- metric moving on its own.
--
-- WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED TO THE FIVE. They carry the exact mapping this header
-- documents, which an unordered LIMIT 1 would not reliably produce — consistent
-- with the real land path (`scripts/land-eas-real.ts`) having written them, and
-- with this file's own "STAGED only, do not apply" instruction having been
-- honoured. They are the five proofs now reported as `ANCHORED_INELIGIBLE`
-- rather than `ANCHORED` (`src/services/anchor-status.ts`): a real attestation
-- over a proof that was never eligible for one. Left alone they read exactly like
-- a genuine anchored proof.
--
-- IF A DEMO NEEDS ANCHORED PROOFS, MINT THEM. `easAnchorWorker` batches to a
-- Merkle root and one attestation covering a hundred proofs measured at roughly
-- $0.0066 in gas. Backfilling a count has never been cheaper than earning it.
--
